const provenanceCopy={
  output:['Publication records','Crossref, DataCite, PubMed, repositories, and other scholarly indexes supply overlapping records.','OpenAlex reconciles identifiers and metadata into Works; Pharos applies the selected institution, dates, and core-corpus scope, then counts the resulting records.'],
  'metadata-patterns':['Metadata coverage','Fields such as DOI, abstract, and source arrive unevenly from publishers, registries, and repositories.','OpenAlex combines the available assertions. Pharos reports presence or absence without treating missing metadata as evidence that the underlying thing does not exist.'],
  'subjects-types':['Inferred classification','Titles, abstracts, citation relationships, and source names provide the classification signals.','OpenAlex predicts Topics with a machine-learning model and rolls the primary Topic into Subfield, Field, and Domain; Pharos aggregates those assignments.'],
  'outputs-access':['Publication and location records','Publishers, DOI agencies, DOAJ, and repositories provide signals about document type and accessible versions.','OpenAlex and Unpaywall now expose the same underlying OA pipeline: OpenAlex checks publisher pages and harvested repository copies, reconciles locations belonging to a Work, and derives open-access status. Pharos reports the saved result; inspect individual records only when that documented method is not sufficient for your intended use.'],
  citations:['Matched reference links','References come from deposited metadata and, for some open works, extracted full text.','OpenAlex matches references to Works and derives citation counts and normalized flags; Pharos reports the saved values without interpreting them as research quality.'],
  venues:['Sources and publishers','Venue names arrive with publication records from Crossref, DataCite, PubMed, repositories, and other feeds.','OpenAlex reconciles them into Sources and publisher lineages; Pharos uses primary locations unless a section explicitly says otherwise.'],
  collaboration:['Authorship affiliations','Authors publish affiliation text, which arrives through publisher, repository, and registry metadata.','OpenAlex parses the text and matches institutions to ROR-backed records. Pharos counts co-occurrence on Works; it does not infer formal partnerships.'],
  funding:['Funding assertions and grant records','Funding mentions come from Work metadata; Award records also come from Crossref, Europe PMC, and national funder databases such as NIH, NSF, CORDIS, and UK Gateway to Research.','OpenAlex reconciles funders, grants, and linked outputs. Missing links are common, and a Work-level acknowledgement does not identify who received an award.'],
  researchers:['Algorithmically resolved people','Names, ORCIDs, affiliations, topics, citations, and co-author patterns arrive on publication records.','OpenAlex clusters those authorships into Author profiles. Pharos filters and ranks the returned profiles; merges and splits can make individual profiles wrong.'],
  affiliations:['Published affiliation text','The displayed strings are the text authors supplied on publications, preserved before institution matching.','OpenAlex’s parser maps strings to institution IDs using models, rules, and ROR. Pharos separates current mappings from plausible name-search candidates; candidates still require human review.'],
  'institution-record':['Organisation registries','Institution identity and hierarchy are grounded primarily in ROR, with additional identifiers and links from sources such as Wikidata.','OpenAlex maintains its Institution entity and connects parsed affiliations to it. Pharos displays those assertions without inventing organisational relationships.']
};
